WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.910
If I showed you Terrance Malick’s most recent
film, Song to Song, along side his debut film

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:11.380
Badlands shot 44 years earlier, they would
seem dramatically different.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.500
Much of what seems to make up the look and
feel of Malick's newer work is the unique

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.521
cinematography developed in collaboration
with Emmanuel Lubezeki Malick’s Director

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.420
of Photography since The New World.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.270
The free-flowing cinematography fits the non-traditional
approach to narrative.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:35.320
And it’s one of the most interesting, most
expressive uses of wide angle lenses I’ve

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.680
seen in film.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.559
But if we look closely at Badlands an everything
that follows, we’ll find many clues that

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:47.610
will help us uncover what motivates the stories
Malick chooses to tell and how he chooses

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.739
to tell them.

